Director/VP, Revenue Operations and Commercial Systems
Remote
eClinical Solutions helps life sciences organizations around the world accelerate clinical development initiatives with expert data services and the elluminate Clinical Data Cloud – the foundation of digital trials. Together, the elluminate platform and digital data services give clients self-service access to all their data from one centralized location plus advanced analytics that help them make smarter, faster business decisions. 

You will make an impact:

We are seeking a commercially focused Revenue Operations leader to bring visibility, structure, and discipline, to eCS’ revenue forecasting, commercial motion, and systems. Reporting to the Chief Financial Officer, this leader will own the systems, data, definitions, reporting, and cadence that drive pipeline visibility, forecast accuracy, and commercial execution across the business, establishing and enforcing common standards across Sales, Finance, Operations, and Product.

The central mandate is to build a high-fidelity, repeatable monitoring and measurement function that can provide visibility into our sales pipeline and funnel, providing the Sales, Finance, and Operations teams with insights that drive decisions supporting attainment of our revenue goals. This role converts our commercial rhythms in a governed, measurable operating model spanning new logo, expansion, and renewal motions across elluminate® licensing, elluminate® services, and Biometrics. This leader will inherit the ongoing Salesforce transformation, complete it, and own the adoption and data discipline that make it useful.

The Chief Business Officer (CBO) remains accountable for the forecast commitment and sales performance. This role owns the machinery that produces the forecast — the process, systems, data, definitions, reporting, and governance behind it. The successful candidate will partner closely with the CBO, the CFO and FP&A team, Customer Success, Product, and the Chief Transformation & AI Officer, and will present recurring commercial reporting to the executive leadership team and the Board.

Accelerate your skills and career within a fast-growing company while impacting the future of healthcare.

Your day to day:

Own Pipeline Discipline & Forecasting:
Define and enforce pipeline stage definitions, entry/exit criteria, forecast categories, and opportunity hygiene standards in Salesforce
Own a standardized forecasting methodology – in partnership with Sales – across licensing, services, and Biometrics, and measure forecast accuracy and bias over time
Own CARR bookings measurement and pipeline-to-bookings conversion; reconcile Salesforce with Finance actuals and resolve discrepancies at the source
Develop and maintain a trusted, repeatable board and executive reporting package in partnership with FP&A
Provide visibility across new logo, expansion, and renewal pipeline
